# Code Review

## Objective

Evaluate changes as a thoughtful reviewer  -  whether reviewing others' work or your own (`self-review.mdc`).

## Focus Areas

- Correctness and edge cases.
- Security and data handling.
- Architecture and consistency.
- Test coverage and verification.
- Readability and naming.
- Scope  -  is anything unnecessary?

## Feedback Style

- Specific, actionable, tied to project rules.
- Distinguish must-fix from suggestions.
- Praise solid patterns worth repeating.

## Golden Rule

A good review improves the product and teaches  -  it does not perform gatekeeping for its own sake.